 "notes": "Single map sheet read from OCR (page 1). Map symbols recorded only where on the same line as the unit name (Qst, Qcbs); other symbols are scattered or garbled in the OCR and were not tied to units. The Water unit was not recorded. Legend-only features (contact, Suffolk Scarp, drill-hole symbol) were not recorded as values. Two values printed with '|' for a digit are read as 1, flagged inferred and sent to review. The Carolina bay text cites Rogers (1977), which is not in the reference list. Units are grouped by the terrace they lie beneath; terrace margin elevations are in each terrace record's contacts.\nSUBSURFACE: cross section A-A' (page 1) is recorded with its vertical exaggeration and datum, but its unit labels (QHfw, QPts, QPtm, QPpm, QPps, Qcb, Qcbs, me...) are OCR'd as scattered rows with no readable distances, and its end points, length and the elevation scale (60/40/20 ft labels) can't be tied to positions, so no units along it were recorded. SCGS drill-hole labels appear on the map face (e.g. 22-102, 22-112, 22-409); the logs are on file at the SCGS and not in this document. Datum: horizontal 1927 North American Datum; topographic contour interval 20 feet on the 1973 base map (page 1).",
